      "note": "The attacker-controlled object stream body parses object 7 as another indirect reference, causing an indirect chain to continue through data just loaded from the stream.",
      "role": "intermediate"
    },
    {
      "step": 4,
      "file": "source/pdf/pdf-xref.c",
      "function": "pdf_load_obj_stm",
      "line": 2134,
      "var": "entry->obj",
      "code": "entry->obj = obj;",
      "note": "The parsed indirect object is stored in the xref cache without keeping a separate resolver-owned reference for the caller that continues chain resolution.",
      "role": "root_cause"
    },
    {
      "step": 5,
      "file": "source/pdf/pdf-xref.c",
      "function": "pdf_resolve_indirect",
      "line": 2570,
      "var": "entry->obj",
      "code": "ref = entry->obj;",
      "note": "The resolver returns the cached object pointer directly, so subsequent chain iterations operate on an object whose lifetime depends on the xref cache being unchanged.",
      "role": "intermediate"
    },
    {
      "step": 6,
      "file": "source/pdf/pdf-xref.c",
      "function": "pdf_resolve_indirect_chain",
      "line": 2580,
      "var": "ref",
      "code": "while (pdf_is_indirect(ctx, ref))",
      "note": "Chain resolution tests the returned pointer as an indirect object after object-stream loading and cache updates, which is the memory-safety access reached by the reproducer.",
      "role": "sink"
    }
  ],
  "vuln_logic": {
    "source": {
      "file": "source/pdf/pdf-xref.c",
      "function": "pdf_read_new_xref_section",
      "line": 1337,
      "operands": ["entry->type", "t"]
